Let \(Y\) denote the number of heads obtained when a fair coin is tossed repeatedly until the first head appears or until \(3\) tosses are completed. Possible outcomes are: \[Y=0 \quad \text{for } TTT\] \[Y=1 \quad \text{for } H,\ TH,\ TTH\] Thus, \[P(Y=0)=\frac{1}{8}\] \[P(Y=1)=1-\frac{1}{8}=\frac{7}{8}\] Now, \[E(Y)=0\cdot \frac{1}{8}+1\cdot \frac{7}{8}
=\frac{7}{8}\] Also, \[E(Y^2)=0^2\cdot \frac{1}{8}+1^2\cdot \frac{7}{8}
=\frac{7}{8}\] Therefore, \[\operatorname{var}(Y)=E(Y^2)-[E(Y)]^2\] \[=\frac{7}{8}-\left(\frac{7}{8}\right)^2\] \[=\frac{56-49}{64}
=\frac{7}{64}\] \[\boxed{\text{(c) } \dfrac{7}{64}}\]

