=\{1,0,-1\}.\] Hence, \[y(n)=x(n)*h(n)=x(n)*\{1,0,-1\}.\] This is equivalent to \[y(n)=x(n)-x(n-2).\] Now test the options. For Option D, \[x(n)=\{1,2,2,1\},\] \[y(n)=\{1,2,1,-1,-2,-1\},\] which exactly matches the given output sequence. \[\boxed{\text{(d) }x(n)=\{1,2,2,1\}}\]

